            "page_id": 10
          }
        ],
        "content": "Tax Anticipation Bills",
        "description": null,
        "id": 3,
        "type": "section_header"
      },
      {
        "bbox": [
          {
            "coord": [
              33,
              418,
              747,
              698
            ],
            "page_id": 10
          }
        ],
        "content": "On June 26 tenders were invited for $2.0 billion, or thereabouts, of 256-day tax anticipation bills and for $2.0 billion, or thereabouts, of 285-day tax anticipation bills, to be issued July 11, 1968. The 256-day bills will mature on March 24, 1969, and the 285-day bills will mature on April 22, 1969, but they will be acceptable at face value in payment of income taxes due on March 15, 1969, and April 15, 1969, respectively. Tenders were opened on July 2.",
        "description": null,
        "id": 4,
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "bbox": [
          {
            "coord": [
              32,
              721,
              746,
              852
            ],
            "page_id": 10
          }
        ],
        "content": "Tenders received for the 256-day bills totaled $4,210 million, of which $2,015 million was accepted. The average bank discount rate was 5.399 percent. The limit for noncompetitive tenders was $400,000. These totaled $277 million.",
        "description": null,
        "id": 5,
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "bbox": [
          {
            "coord": [
              33,
              876,
              749,
              1012
            ],
            "page_id": 10
          }
        ],
        "content": "Tenders received for the 285-day bills totaled $4,026 million, of which $2,003 million was accepted. The average bank discount rate was 5.426 percent. The limit for noncompetitive tenders was $400,000. These totaled $234 million.",
        "description": null,
        "id": 6,
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "bbox": [
          {
            "coord": [
              37,
              1037,
              749,
              1206
            ],
            "page_id": 10
          }
        ],
        "content": "All bidders for either issue were required to agree not to purchase or to sell, or to make any agreements with respect to the purchase or sale or other disposition of any bills of that issue at a specific rate or price, until after one-thirty p.m., Eastern daylight saving time, July 2, 1968.",
        "description": null,
        "id": 7,
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "bbox": [
          {
            "coord": [
              35,
              1234,
              747,
              1363
            ],
            "page_id": 10
          }
        ],
        "content": "Any qualified depositary was permitted to make payment by credit in its Treasury tax and loan account for bills allotted to it for itself and its customers up to any amount for which it was qualified in excess of existing deposits.",
        "description": null,
        "id": 8,
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
